<title>URUGUAY: Uruguay's foreign debt rises to $2.14 bln in June.</title>
<headline>Uruguay's foreign debt rises to $2.14 bln in June.</headline>
<dateline>MONTEVIDEO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uruguay's net foreign debt rose 4.4 percent to $2.14 billion at the end of June from $2.05 billion in May, the Central Bank said Wednesday.</p>
<p>However, it dropped 1.3 percent from the end of 1995, when it stood at $2.17 billion.</p>
<p>Foreign reserves stood at $2.60 billion in June, up from $2.56 billion in May and $2.49 billion by December 31.</p>
<p>-- Esteban Israel, Montevideo Newsroom + 5982 92 03 36</p>
</text>
